Package: baGWAS
Type: Package
Title: Genome-Wide Association Analysis with Genotype- and Frequency-Based
    Strategies
Version: 1.0.5
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohammad", "Fallahi", email = "mohammad.fallahi@modares.ac.ir",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Dani", "Fayazi-Kia", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Provides a reproducible workflow for genome-wide association
    analysis using two strategies: genotype-based GWAS (genoGWAS) with
    GEMMA linear mixed models and frequency-based GWAS (freqGWAS) using
    allele-frequency matrices, group-level relationships, and EMMREML.
    The package prepares input files, runs PLINK and GEMMA, performs scans,
    creates Manhattan and Q-Q plots, writes run logs, and returns a
    standardized result data frame.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
OS_type: unix
Imports:
    data.table,
    EMMREML,
    ggplot2,
    ggmanh,
    parallel,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: PLINK 1.9/2.0 and GEMMA (external executables)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
